<title>USA: Spelling Entertainment CFO resigns.</title>
<headline>Spelling Entertainment CFO resigns.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spelling Entertainment Group Inc said Wednesday Chief Financial Officer William Clark has resigned &quot;to pursue other interests.&quot;</p>
<p>Clark joined the company in November 1996.</p>
<p>The company said that on an interim basis, Clark's responsibilities will be shared by James Miller, the company's vice president, controller and chief accounting officer, and Ross Landsbaum, vice president of finance and tax.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
</text>
